 "news": {
  "date": "2026-09-18",
  "asof": "2026-09-21 10:27 UTC",
  "headline": "The Bank of Japan hiked to a 31-year high and the yen fell \u2014 and $7 trillion expired without moving anything",
  "standfirst": "The BoJ raised to 1.25%, its highest since 1995, on a 7-2 split with Ueda refusing to commit to a pace \u2014 and USD/JPY pushed back above 157. A dovish hike is the one outcome the carry trade was not hedged for: the US-Japan gap is wider this morning, not narrower. In New York about $7 trillion of options exposure expired, the second largest on record, and the largest move on the board was 0.64 sigma. The S&P rose 0.17% to 7,650.50, the Nasdaq 0.39%, the Dow fell 0.18% and the Russell 0.50%. The ten-year went back to 5.00% and the two-year set another 52-week high, so Thursday\u2019s bond rally lasted exactly one session. In the book OKTA fell 4.05% to 182.32, back below its fill, giving back the whole of Monday\u2019s move \u2014 with its stop never within 11% of being touched. Heat 3.05R against 3.0R, unchanged all week.",
  "themes": [
   {
