    "note": "<b>Oktane is Wednesday</b>, and the timing is awkward in a useful way. OKTA closed the week 41 cents below its entry after a 4% expiry-day fall, its CEO spent Tuesday on television setting the event up, and the stock trades a shade below the street's average target. An investor summit is where a management team either justifies a re-rating or fails to. This is the only holding with a scheduled reason to move before late October."
